Spake thus Forest Sprite:

>Worse writing (though less clause-heavy) from the Washington Post, Metro
>section, Dec. 6th:
>
>"The head of a Northeast Washington charter school at the center of a
>controversy over a tussle with a reporter portrayed herself as having a
>passion for molding young blacks and being unafraid of confrontations with
>institutions that she sees standing in her way."

In Lojban:

lo ralju belo'i xe nupre ckule nela nortist. .uacint,n. be'o
poi se nunpro folenu jairda'a belo ternuzba cu skuski vo'a foleka
xaurga'i loi citno xekre'a kei jo'u leka nalte'a lenu fapro
loi truci'e poi pe'idai jai zunti tu'a ry.

Interesting to note are the particles "be'o", "kei" and "cu" that delimit the
scope of phrases and enable the relative clause to attach to the correct
argument.

